      "writtenOn": "2023-06-29T04:05:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Actually, they are meant to be generic. Although I use Butterworth LPF here, the filter_iir_t can be high-, low-, or band- pass depending on the a and b parameters. By choosing different a%b the filter can become Chebyshev filter, Elliptic or any other IIR design.\n \nI can change it to filter_iir_init and filter_iir_step to indicate the class of filter types the function supports.",
      "parentUuid": "74496d94_a791eab8",
      "revId": "f4117c9a1f37c174610e10667a2cbd877d40a900",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
